  "plan": {
    "goal": "Recapitulate the resting wall shear of the human proximal pulmonary artery on an endothelial-lined microfluidic channel.",
    "rationale": "The human proximal pulmonary artery resting wall shear is commonly cited at ~0.5 Pa (5 dyn/cm²), within the HUVEC/microvascular endothelial physiological range (0.1-1 Pa, per cell_physiology). A 400 µm wide x 100 µm high x 20 mm long PDMS channel at 20 µL/min delivers 0.5 Pa wall shear (verified via wall_shear_stress). Flow is laminar (Re ~1.3), pressure drop ~200 Pa (well within syringe-pump range), residence time ~2.4 s. HUVEC seeded at 15,000 cells/cm² on the 0.08 cm² channel floor (~1,200 cells) gives a confluent endothelial monolayer. Medium viscosity assumed water-like (1e-3 Pa·s).",
