    "caveats": [
      "Verify the resting proximal pulmonary artery shear target (~0.5 Pa) against the specific literature/clinical source you intend to cite; values in the literature range ~0.3-1.5 Pa depending on vessel segment and measurement method.",
      "Confirm HUVEC (or a pulmonary-artery-specific endothelial line) is the intended cell source; the registry maps pulmonary artery endothelium to HUVEC.",
      "Coat the channel (e.g. fibronectin/collagen) and confirm a confluent monolayer before flow; seed at the upper end of the 10-20k cells/cm² range if attachment is poor.",
      "Check the syringe pump can deliver 20 µL/min stably against the ~200 Pa backpressure; use a low-dead-volume line.",
      "Confirm medium viscosity (~1e-3 Pa·s); serum-supplemented medium is close to water but verify if using high-viscosity additives.",
      "Endothelial health readout should be morphology/junctional markers (e.g. VE-cadherin), not TEER, which is low for HUVEC."
    ]
  },
